## 5b. Value chain what-if simulator — commodity-specific adaptation (REQUIRED)

The gold value chain what-if simulator (`value_chain/what_if_simulator.html`) is built around
gold-specific controls and calculations.  **Every non-gold project must replace these entirely.**

### Controls to replace

| Gold element | Replace with (example for AUBEB) |
|---|---|
| AISC slider (`min=900 max=2200`) | Primary price slider for this commodity (e.g. carbon credit price $5–$80) |
| Cash cost slider | Secondary cost/floor control relevant to the commodity |
| Spot price slider | Market price or contract price relevant to this commodity |
| Entity selector (`Newmont E001`, `Barrick E002`) | Project-specific entities from PDI `A7_actor_classes`, or Phase selector |
| `ref_production_oz_per_year` parameter | Equivalent production unit from PDI `programme_scale` (ha, tCO₂e/yr, kg/yr, etc.) |
| `carbon_cost_per_oz` / `energy_cost_per_oz` | Costs denominated in the commodity's native unit |
| `stabilityIndex(price, aisc, cash)` function | Stability function using the commodity's margin structure |

### Derived outputs to recalculate

Replace gold financial outputs with outputs meaningful for the commodity:

| Gold output | AUBEB equivalent | Shea equivalent |
|---|---|---|
| Margin vs AISC | Net carbon revenue (price × tCO₂e/yr − costs) | Net value to women (retail − farm-gate) |
| Breakeven price | Carbon floor to cover project costs | Farm-gate breakeven |
| Spread (AISC − Cash) | CORSIA floor − VCM floor spread | Margin per MT |
| Stability index | Programme financial resilience score | Value chain equity score |

### Data source

The simulator should load from the same files as the dashboard:
- `<m>_value_metrics.json` for price/cost baseline values
- `<m>_value_ndc_metrics.json` for D/C/N initial slider positions

### Reference implementations

- **Gold**: `frontend/project/gold/value_chain/what_if_simulator.html` — AISC/cash-cost model
- **Shea**: `frontend/project/shea/value_chain/what_if_simulator.html` — price-to-women + carbon credit model
- Use the shea implementation as a closer template for non-extractive / nature-based projects.

---

## 5c. Value chain financial report — commodity-specific adaptation (REQUIRED)

The gold financial report (`value_chain/financial_report.html`) uses a mining income-statement
structure: AISC sub-components, Newmont/Barrick entities, realized price per troy oz, Phase 1
cash costs, royalties, sustaining capex, etc.  **All of this must be replaced per commodity.**

### Income statement structure by commodity type

| Commodity type | Revenue lines | Cost lines | Key ratio |
|---|---|---|---|
| Extractive (gold) | Realized price × oz produced | Cash cost/oz, AISC/oz, royalties | AISC margin |
| Agricultural (shea) | Farm-gate price × kg, retail uplift | Processing margin/kg, logistics | Value-to-women ratio |
| Nature-based / carbon (AUBEB) | VCM price × tCO₂e/yr, CORSIA premium | Restoration cost/ha, MRV fees, certification | Net programme surplus |
| Other commodities | Derive from PDI `pricing_reference` and `multi_value_outputs` | Derive from PDI `phase_cost_estimates` | Margin relative to breakeven price |

### Entity selector

Replace gold company entities with entities appropriate to the commodity:
- **Carbon projects**: Phase selector or single programme entity from PDI `A7_actor_classes`
- **Agricultural**: buyer/aggregator entities from PDI, or cooperative vs. market scenarios

### Key lines to replace in the copied HTML

| Gold element | Replace with |
|---|---|
| `Realized Mangrove/Gold Price ($/oz)` | Primary revenue metric for this commodity ($/tCO₂e, $/kg, etc.) |
| `Annual Production (oz/yr)` | Programme throughput unit from PDI (`tCO₂e/yr`, `ha`, `kg/yr`) |
| `AISC` and `Cash Cost` sub-components | Cost structure relevant to this commodity's PDI phases |
| `Royalties & Production Taxes` | Applicable levies (e.g. carbon registry fees, government sharing) |
| `Sustaining Capital Expenditure` | Ongoing investment type (e.g. monitoring equipment, replanting) |
| `Reclamation & Closure Accrual` | Programme-end obligations (if applicable) |
| `Phase 2–8 costs` headers | Rename to match actual PDI phase names |
| Carbon price slider ($/tCO₂e) | Keep if commodity has a carbon co-benefit; remove if not applicable |
| `t/oz` emissions intensity metric | Replace with commodity-native denominator (t/ha, kg CO₂/kg, etc.) |

### Supply chain pages — data source citations

When copying supply chain pages (dashboard, emissions analysis, energy analysis, water analysis,
what-if simulator), they may carry incidental references to the source commodity's benchmark data
(e.g. "Newmont 2024 SR", "WGC 2023", "t/oz", "ICMM Water Reporting Guidelines").

These must be updated to cite sources appropriate to the new commodity:
- Replace corporate benchmark citations (Newmont, Barrick, WGC) with sources from PDI
  `sources_overview` and `module_4_opacity`.
- Replace `t/oz` intensity denominators with the commodity-native unit.
- Where no real data exists, mark as `"benchmark estimate — not project-specific"`.

